{"ts": 1784344215.539142, "event": "finish", "summary": "Held the entire window. Price dipped modestly in the first ~5m (to about -5.75pts) but never showed a sustained breakdown, then trended strongly favorable, cresting near +129pts before settling in the +75-92pts range by the end of the window -- always well above entry after minute 8. Nothing in the sequence looked like a wrong-direction entry: pullbacks were giveback off local favorable peaks, not drawdowns through entry, and the leg amplitude/giveback pattern matched normal profit-taking chop, not a reversal. Next time I'd watch for a pullback that actually breaches back through 0 (entry) after a strong favorable run, or a giveback% that keeps climbing past ~150-200% while price is also making lower highs on the 1m/5m closed bars -- that combination would be the real wrong-direction tell, not just a same-direction retrace.", "exit_frame": null, "n_commits": 44}
